<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The Unaudited  CFS for the Qtr and 9M ended 31.12.2019 have been prepared in accordance with the Co. (Ind AS) Rules, 2015 prescribed under Sec 133 of the Co. Act, 2013 and guidelines under SEBI (LODR) Reg 2015, as amended. 2. And were reviewed by the Audit Committee, approved  and  taken on record by the Board at its meeting held on 14.02.2020.  The Statutory Auditors have carried out a Ltd Review of the aforesaid results in terms of Reg 33 of LODR, 3.As amended, the Company has disclosed Consolidated Quarterly Results from the QE 30.06.2019.  The CFS of the corresponding periods are management certified figures. 4.The CFS relate to W.S. Industries (India) Limited (the Parent Company) (WSI), and its Subsidiary Companies (SC). The WSI with its SCs constitute the Group. 5.The SCs considered in the CFS are W.S. T &amp; D Ltd (WSTD) (till the date of cessation of control on  09.06.2019) and Vidagara Tech Park Private Limited. Country of incorp. is India and the % of voting power by WSI is 0.13% and 100% respectively as on 31.12.2019. 6.The conversion of Series B Debentures allotted by WSTD into equity shares on 10.06.2019 resulted  in the cessation of control of the Holding Company (HC) in WSTD. This is accordingly reflected  in the books of the Company under Ind AS110 in CFS for the QE 30.06.2019. 7.No production and related activities were carried out  by HC during the period. 8.No Interest has been provided on the facilities availed from financial institutions by the HC during the period under review. 9. The HC intends to sell/transfer its Insulator Manufacturing Plant at Visakhapatnam (Vizag) (reported on 14.01.2020). As part of this transaction, the Secured Lenders (SL) have agreed to waive interest amount of Rs.25 Cr. once payment is made to them arising from the sale/transfer of the Vizag Plant. The waiver of Interest by  each individual SL shall be proportionate to the amounts  received by such lender. 10. The HC has identified its Chennai Unit and Vizag Unit (3 months from QE Dec 2019) under Ind AS 105 and accordingly adjustments are shown separately in the statement of P&amp;L. Hence previous period figures are not comparable. 11. The Group is not required to provide Segment Reporting under the criteria specified in IND AS 108. 12. Impairment to the extent of  Rs.45.75 Cr. has been provided in the books of Vizag of the HC, comprising of  Land on unexpired Lease period (as on 31.12.2019), Buildings on Card Rate and other fixed assets on the respective WDV basis. 13. The HC has partially complied with  the terms of the settlement agreements executed with the SL as highlighted in the annual report for the FY ending 31.03.2019 but the company has been unable to complete the full and final settlement due in Feb. 2019.  Pursuant to the same, the  HC has received latest claim letter received in  Jan. 2020 claiming repayment of contractual dues as follows as on 31.12.2019: (i)   Rs.427.41 cr., from Edelweiss Asset Reconstruction Co. Ltd (in its capacity as Trustee of EARC SAF 1 Trust, EARC Trust SC 168, EARC Trust SC 209). (ii) Rs.84.09 cr., from IDBI Trusteeship Service Ltd (as a debenture trustee on behalf of NCD holders) and (iii) Rs.133.67 cr., from Allium Finance Pvt Ltd. The claim amounts include interest up to the said period  and other charges  as provided for under the respective financing documents entered into by the HC. The HC is in discussions with the SL for its resolution. 14. Fair Value assessment on the Investment in equity shares of RMZ One Paramount Ltd (erstwhile WSTD) is Negative as on 31.12.2019 and hence the carrying cost is considered as Rs.1/-. .Net Fair Value loss of Rs.5.01 Lakhs has been provided in the books of Chennai Unit of the HC. 15. Inventories comprising of Raw Materials, Stores and Spares, WIP, Finished Goods  and Capital WIP have been written off in the books of the HC to the extent of Rs.41.18 lakhs in Chennai division and Rs.143.53 lakhs in Vizag divison because of  Discontinued Operations .</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
